WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.112
Let’s walk through RFIs.

00:00:02.112 --> 00:00:04.325
Use an RFI when the team needs a ruling,

00:00:04.325 --> 00:00:07.175
clarification, or missing scenario fact.

00:00:07.175 --> 00:00:10.700
State one decision-blocking question with enough context to answer,

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:13.700
and revise the same record if White Cell returns it

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:13.825
.

00:00:13.825 --> 00:00:16.212
On this slide, send a focused request when the

00:00:16.212 --> 00:00:20.050
team needs a ruling, clarification, or scenario detail

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:20.212
.

00:00:20.212 --> 00:00:24.150
In practice, include enough context to unblock one decision

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:24.275
.

00:00:24.275 --> 00:00:27.262
If White Cell returns it, revise the same RFI

00:00:27.262 --> 00:00:29.288
rather than creating a duplicate.

00:00:29.785 --> 00:00:32.685
When you are ready, use Open RFIs to move

00:00:32.685 --> 00:00:34.160
to the live surface.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:36.860
The guide will not make the workflow decision for you

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:37.010
.
